  "caveats": [
    "All seventeen Java suites run in one fresh isolated build. Source/POM inventory, compiled artifacts, retained raw files and complete Python normal/optimized suites are bound separately.",
    "Twelve actual public-bootstrap histories cover 3/4/5 voters, EMPTY/backup, lower proposer and lower follower. Two additional real unpublished accepted-tail histories cover both directions at size three. Current batch reopening is same-JVM; existing owner recovery regressions supply their separately scoped fresh-process/crash evidence.",
    "Exact original sources are fixed before missing proof I/O. Authenticated complete current-prefix/manifest/ancestry can prove the unchanged original BASIS packet without producing a new historical vote or changing its accepted tail.",
    "Install other selected remotes before the longest remote generation, then install locally. Complete original/received images may be borrowed only through actual pinned physical owners; old local backing sources remain pinned through the original export lifetime. Borrowed images never expand remote source inventory.",
    "Five deterministic new proof faults and received/retained image ownership tests supplement normal original-first physical/image replay, exact mutations, optimized replay and relocated archive replay. Component evidence does not close an entire protocol family.",
    "Earlier missing-ancestry, lost local key, union-image, longest-generation lifetime, compilation, accepted-tail capacity and oracle duplicate-control failures are retained. Prior-source successes are diagnostic evidence only and never substitute for this final qualification.",
    "Campaigns are explicitly invoked. Autonomous election/discovery/adoption, repeated maintenance, native cross-view pending contexts, learner/joint transitions, generalized publication and the complete 3B\u20133E gate remain open.",
    "No public factory, persisted format, resource/deadline bound, POM, workflow, V5.2 Runner, push, paid cloud or release change."
  ],
